## 1️⃣ Backend Python Files

### [mental_health_api.py](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/mental_health_api.py)
**Type**: Backend - REST API Server  
**Purpose**: Main Flask application that serves as the backend API server

**Key Features**:
- REST API endpoints for text analysis
- WebSocket support for real-time chat
- Session management
- Integration with AI models and crisis detection

**Package Dependencies**:
```python
flask                 # Web framework
flask-cors           # Cross-origin resource sharing
flask-socketio       # WebSocket support for real-time communication
numpy                # Numerical operations
```

**Key Classes/Functions**:
- [MentalHealthChatAPI](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/mental_health_api.py#17-113): Main API class handling chat sessions
- [analyze_message()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/mental_health_api.py#67-113): Analyzes individual chat messages
- REST endpoints: `/api/health`, `/api/analyze`, `/api/resources`
- WebSocket events: `send_message`, [join_session](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/mental_health_api.py#288-298)

**Imports From Other Project Files**:
- `hybrid_classifier.HybridMentalHealthClassifier`
- `crisis_detection.CrisisDetectionSystem`

---

### [hybrid_classifier.py](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/hybrid_classifier.py)
**Type**: Backend - AI Model Architecture  
**Purpose**: Implements the hybrid transformer architecture for mental health classification

**Key Features**:
- Dual BERT model architecture (MentalBERT + MentalRoBERTa)
- Cascaded CNN layers for feature extraction
- 4-class classification (Depression, Anxiety, BPD, PTSD)

**Package Dependencies**:
```python
tensorflow           # Deep learning framework
transformers         # Hugging Face transformers (BERT models)
numpy                # Array operations
```

**Key Classes/Functions**:
- [HybridMentalHealthClassifier](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/hybrid_classifier.py#7-270): Main model class
- [build_model()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/hybrid_classifier.py#96-191): Constructs the hybrid architecture
- [create_cnn_branch()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/hybrid_classifier.py#34-95): Creates CNN feature extraction layers
- [prepare_inputs()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/hybrid_classifier.py#219-248): Tokenizes text for BERT models

**Model Architecture**:
1. **Input**: Text (max 512 tokens)
2. **Branch 1**: MentalBERT → 3 CNN layers → 384-dim features
3. **Branch 2**: MentalRoBERTa → 3 CNN layers → 384-dim features
4. **Fusion**: Concatenate → Dense layers → 4-class output

---

### [crisis_detection.py](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/crisis_detection.py)
**Type**: Backend - Safety System  
**Purpose**: Real-time crisis detection and intervention for suicidal ideation and self-harm

**Key Features**:
- Keyword-based crisis detection (HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW risk levels)
- Emergency notification system
- Safety plan generation
- Multi-country crisis hotline resources

**Package Dependencies**:
```python
re                   # Regular expressions for pattern matching
numpy                # Numerical operations
smtplib              # Email notifications (emergency alerts)
```

**Key Classes/Functions**:
- [CrisisDetectionSystem](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/crisis_detection.py#8-377): Main crisis detection class
- [detect_crisis_level()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/crisis_detection.py#60-98): Analyzes text for crisis indicators
- [generate_crisis_response()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/crisis_detection.py#142-210): Provides appropriate crisis resources
- [send_emergency_notification()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/crisis_detection.py#211-257): Sends alerts to emergency contacts

**Crisis Keywords Monitored**:
- **CRITICAL**: "kill myself", "end my life", "suicide plan"
- **HIGH**: "want to die", "self-harm", "cutting"
- **MEDIUM**: "hopeless", "worthless", "can't go on"

---

### [explainable_ai.py](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/explainable_ai.py)
**Type**: Backend - Model Interpretability  
**Purpose**: Provides explanations for AI predictions using multiple techniques

**Key Features**:
- Attention weight visualization from BERT layers
- LIME (Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations)
- Word importance scoring
- HTML report generation with highlighted text

**Package Dependencies**:
```python
tensorflow           # For model inference
transformers         # BERT tokenizers
numpy                # Array operations
matplotlib           # Visualization
seaborn              # Statistical plotting
lime                 # Model explanation library
shap                 # SHapley Additive exPlanations
```

**Key Classes/Functions**:
- [ExplainableAI](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/explainable_ai.py#9-335): Main explainability class
- [get_attention_weights()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/explainable_ai.py#27-50): Extracts BERT attention patterns
- [explain_with_lime()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/explainable_ai.py#77-114): Generates LIME explanations
- [comprehensive_explanation_report()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/explainable_ai.py#288-335): Creates full explanation report

