### [model_trainer.py](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py)
**Type**: Backend - Training Pipeline  
**Purpose**: Handles model training, evaluation, and performance visualization

**Key Features**:
- Training loop with callbacks (early stopping, model checkpointing)
- Performance metrics calculation (accuracy, precision, recall, F1)
- Confusion matrix visualization
- ROC curve plotting
- Training history visualization

**Package Dependencies**:
```python
tensorflow           # Deep learning framework
numpy                # Numerical operations
matplotlib           # Plotting
seaborn              # Statistical visualization
sklearn              # Metrics and evaluation tools
pandas               # Data handling
```

**Key Classes/Functions**:
- [ModelTrainer](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py#10-308): Main training class
- [train()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py#64-107): Trains the model with validation
- [evaluate()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py#142-198): Computes test metrics
- [plot_confusion_matrix()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py#199-254): Visualizes classification results
- [plot_training_history()](file:///c:/Users/SAI/Desktop/Major-project/model_trainer.py#108-141): Shows loss/accuracy curves

**Training Configuration** (from paper):
- Epochs: 40
- Batch size: 64
- Learning rate: 0.001
- Optimizer: Adam

